<title>FRANCE: CFF sells hotels and holiday villages.</title>
<headline>CFF sells hotels and holiday villages.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Foncier de France said it had concluded the sale of its holiday and hotel activities to the U.S. investment fund Whitehall and Westmont Hospitality Group for an undisclosed price.</p>
<p>The units sold are Soderetour, which manages the Citadines appartment hotels and Eurimeg which has apartment hotels in Barcelona, London and Brussels.</p>
<p>Whitehall is managed by Goldman Sachs.</p>
</text>
